    "body": "Findings (agent, M5): I tried the `top - step` change and am releasing the claim. It is bigger than one helper.\n\n**What I tried:** in `cut_levels` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/levels.rs`), start at `z = top - stepdown` instead of `z = top`. The helper tests for that change pass. I then ran `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app`.\n\n**Result:** about 95 tests fail across about 30 binaries, and 18 CL goldens move. Most failures are level-count and Z pins that would simply be re-pinned. Three are real safety laws, where downstream logic depends on the ladder having a level at Top:\n\n- `app blind_floor::random_stepdowns_and_floors_never_cut_below_a_floor`, case 4: a hole floor less than one step below Top (top 20, floor 16.1) gets **no ring at all** (`[] vs floor 16.1`). The old Top level was clamped down to the floor; with it gone, the hole goes uncut.\n- `app area_open::a_containment_that_puts_the_tool_in_the_part_is_caught_by_the_depth_aware_verify`: the default bore-wall contour is refused (\"every contour ring cuts into the part at its first level\"). That law reads level 0 as Top.\n- `motion blind_floor::a_blind_pocket_never_enters_solid_under_any_ladder`: a 3 mm-deep Waterline pocket under a 4 mm step reports \"nothing to cut: the model fills the pocket at every level\".\n\n**A further concern for the owner's question:** when Top is set *below* the material top, the old level at Top cut from the stock top down to Top in one bite. Starting at `top - step` makes that first bite one step deeper still. So \"skip the Top level only when Top is at or above the material top\" is the safer rule, but the ladder helper does not know the material top today.\n\n**Recommendation:** keep the ladder as it is until the owner answers the question. If it goes ahead, the work is one deliberate PR that (1) gives the floor clamp (blind rings and the waterline pocket) a \"first level below Top, or the floor if the floor is shallower than one step\" rule, (2) moves the first-level laws in contour containment off \"level 0 = Top\", and (3) re-pins and re-blesses everything in one commit. Nothing is pushed; the trial diff is only the 3-line change above.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
