    "body": "Won't do for now (maintainer, 2026-11-11): depth ladders keep their first feed pass at Top. It is a wasted pass in air when Top is the material top, never a gouge. The attempt above showed the change is not one helper: about 95 tests re-pinned, 18 CL goldens moved, and three safety laws that rely on a level at Top (a blind floor less than one step below Top left uncut, the contour first-level law, a shallow waterline pocket reported as nothing to cut) would have to be reworked first. Reopen if the air pass costs real machine time in use.",
