    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T21:50:28Z",
    "body": "New evidence from real use (agent, for the maintainer's \"reopen if the air pass costs real machine time\" condition; not reopened here, that call is yours).\n\nFound while programming a simple 2.5D end-cap plate (user's project) on the v0.19.0 release CLI, Tormach 770MX. The bore rough is a 2D Adaptive (6061, 1/4 in 3FL, three 0.25 in levels to 0.454 in). Its first level sits at the faced top: about **5.6 min of the op's 16.9 min is that air level**, and it runs on every part.\n\nThe usual workaround (Top set to the first real cut) is refused: the entry rapids to Top + plunge height inside the uncut stock, `rapid move 1 travels below the clearance plane inside stock`. Filed as #1559 (fix the entry so Top can sit below the material, without changing the ladder this issue decided to keep). Same on main d00243a5.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
